WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:58.480
OK, let's set the scene. Kazakhstan is

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:01.199
really huge—it's the size of Western

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:03.680
Europe. It's also pretty wealthy. It has

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:06.080
the biggest economy in Central Asia and

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:08.720
huge reserves of oil, natural gas and

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.960
minerals. Thing is most people in

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:13.200
Kazakhstan don't really benefit from

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.520
that wealth. The average person earns

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:18.000
less than $600 a month

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.720
and then there's a small group of super

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.799
rich tycoons.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:25.280
162 people own around 50% of the

00:01:22.799 --> 00:01:28.720
country's wealth, according to one report.

00:01:36.159 --> 00:01:41.119
And for decades, there's

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:45.759
been one guy at the very top of that

00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:45.759
system—Nursultan Nazarbayev.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:51.040
He was a leading official back when

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:52.640
Kazakhstan was part of the Soviet Union

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:57.119
and then became president after

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:59.680
Kazakhstan got its independence in 1991.

00:01:57.119 --> 00:02:00.560
Nazarbayev held on to the job for 30

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.640
years.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.719
No real political opposition was allowed

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.960
to emerge and basically everything

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:09.360
revolved around him. 

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.040
But in 2019

00:02:28.879 --> 00:02:33.760
Nazarbayev finally stepped down as

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:36.959
president and his hand-picked successor,

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:40.000
Kassym-Jomart Tokayev, became president—

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:42.640
in name anyway. Because Nazarbayev stuck

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:45.040
around. He kept his title of Elbasy—

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.480
that's "leader of the nation" and got a

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.879
lifetime appointment to head up

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.560
Kazakhstan's powerful Security Council.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.319
But still, with Tokayev taking over as president,

00:03:00.159 --> 00:03:05.040
there was a sense that change was in the

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:06.879
air. He promised to bring in some reforms

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.040
and even went on what he called a

00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:11.519
listening tour around the country.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.200
Trouble is, things didn't really change.

00:03:22.239 --> 00:03:26.319
So when people woke up on the

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:28.799
first day of 2022 and saw that fuel

00:03:26.319 --> 00:03:31.799
prices had doubled, well, that got people

00:03:28.799 --> 00:03:31.799
going.

00:03:32.159 --> 00:03:37.280
The protests started off peacefully in a

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:39.760
town in the west.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:41.280
But within days they'd spread across the

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.040
country.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:45.440
And even though the government quickly

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:48.080
reversed the fuel-price hike, by this

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:51.080
point the anger had become about so much

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:51.080
more.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:29.320
Things soon got violent, especially in

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.320
Kazakhstan's biggest city, Almaty.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:35.520
President Tokayev declared a state of

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:37.919
emergency and blamed what he called

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:39.520
terrorists, bandits and foreign actors

00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:41.680
for what was happening, although he

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.840
didn't give any evidence and he said

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.840
this:

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:14.880
Here's something else Tokayev

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:17.520
did. He called for outside help from a

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:19.199
regional military alliance led by Russia.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:21.840
It's called the Collective Security

00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:24.800
Treaty Organization–the CSTO.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:27.840
And it responded with around 2,500

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:30.560
soldiers, mostly Russians. 

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:53.120
In any case, the crackdown seemed

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:55.280
to work. Within about a week things had

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.960
calmed down and those foreign troops

00:05:55.280 --> 00:06:00.000
were on their way home.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:02.080
The government said 225 people had been

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.120
killed, including 19 members of the

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:07.199
security forces. Around 12,000 people

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:09.600
have been arrested, so far.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:25.759
Now, there's something else going on here and

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:27.919
that's all the political intrigue and

00:06:25.759 --> 00:06:28.720
what looks like a power struggle at the

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:30.800
top.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:33.360
Remember how we said that when Tokayev

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:35.600
became president, Nazarbayev was still

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:37.919
pulling the strings? Well, it looks like

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:40.479
things have shifted. During this whole

00:06:37.919 --> 00:06:42.400
time Nazarbayev was nowhere to be seen.

00:06:40.479 --> 00:06:45.280
There were even rumours he'd fled the

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:49.400
country, rumours he eventually denied in a

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:49.400
video statement on his website.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:12.319
Now, in that statement Nazarbayev also

00:07:10.319 --> 00:07:14.880
denied there were any divisions at the

00:07:12.319 --> 00:07:16.880
top, but one thing looks pretty clear—

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:19.520
Tokayev seems to have strengthened his

00:07:16.880 --> 00:07:21.599
position. Tokayev took Nazarbayev's job

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:23.680
as head of the Security Council, and a

00:07:21.599 --> 00:07:25.840
close ally of Nazarbayev, the head of the

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:28.560
intelligence agency, was arrested for

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:31.520
treason. Tokayev also appointed a new

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:33.520
prime minister and a new cabinet.

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:36.319
But the big question is what this

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:38.400
actually means for people in Kazakhstan.

00:07:36.319 --> 00:07:40.639
Are they going to see things change? He

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:43.039
announced a bunch of new policies, things

00:07:40.639 --> 00:07:45.360
like higher taxes for mining companies

00:07:43.039 --> 00:07:48.080
and a new social fund that the richest

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:52.319
people and companies are meant to pay into.

00:08:16.319 --> 00:08:21.120
What we've seen with the recent events in Kazakhstan are the

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:23.680
first big signs of cracks in the system—

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:25.520
the old way of doing things. Tokayev

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:28.800
seems to be trying to paper over those

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:32.159
cracks, but will it work? And for how long?

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:51.920
